[bug · medium] The newly-extracted `_typed` helper opens `connect.connect(client.app.state.db_path,
read_only=True)` and only calls `connect.close(conn)` after a successful SELECT. If the SELECT
raises (corrupt DB, schema mismatch, unexpected rows), the file-based read-only connection is
leaked. The staging module's own `Stage.restore` comment explicitly warns about this case ("a
connection a test leaked still holds the -wal open on Windows, and the backup writes the destination
through its own pager with such connections present"), and `connect.connect` returns a plain
`Connection` rather than a context manager (db/connect.py:152), so `with connect.connect(...) as
conn:` is not available. Wrap the SELECT in `try: ... finally: connect.close(conn)` — the pattern is
the same shape already used in `tests/staging.py:407-418` (`migrated`).

