─── tests/staging.py:732-744 ───
[bug · medium] _rebuilt_none() is the last statement of the `finally` clause in both `hosting()` and
`staged()`, so its AssertionError REPLACES any test failure raised during the `yield` instead of
being reported alongside it. A test that legitimately fails AND happens to leave the library mutated
will surface only the rebuild assertion, hiding the actual failure (and the rebuild's likely role as
cleanup that never ran). Use `raise AssertionError(...) from exc` or skip the assertion when an
exception is already in flight.



