[bug · medium] Latent test-isolation bug from the move to module-scoped `_world`.
`test_a_file_with_no_decodable_frame_is_a_404_not_a_500` (around line 438) writes `broken.mp4` into
the staged library root and never removes it. Under the old per-test `served` fixture, that file
died with `tmp_path`; under the new module-scoped one, the library directory is shared across all
tests. Because `_world` is declared with `keep_thumbs=True` and the default `rebuilds=0`, any
subsequent test in this module that calls `served` (which calls `_world.restore()`) will see
`_listing(self.root) != self.library`, force a rebuild, increment `stage.rebuilds`, and trip the
`_rebuilt_none` teardown assertion. The bug is masked only because this test happens to be the LAST
one in source order; any test added after it, any reordering, or any `pytest-randomly`-style shuffle
will surface it. Fix: clean up `broken.mp4` at the end of the broken-frame test (try/finally, or
write to a per-test tmp_path), or move the file outside the staged library root.



