[bug · medium] `_read_record()` only catches `FileNotFoundError` and `json.JSONDecodeError`, but
`path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")` can also raise `PermissionError`, `IsADirectoryError`, or
`UnicodeDecodeError` (none of which subclass the two caught), and `json.loads(...)` can return any
JSON value (e.g. `None`, list, string) without raising. The function's annotation `-> dict` is
therefore a lie: it can return `None`/list/str, and `provisioned()` then does `.get(...)` on it,
raising `AttributeError` and turning the supposed-fast offline guard into a 500 instead of a clean
refusal. Broaden the `except` to catch the I/O subclasses (`OSError`, `UnicodeDecodeError`) and
validate the parsed value is a dict before returning it.



